<title>GREECE: BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS BASE DRACHMA LOAN RATE TO 17.5PCT.</title>
<headline>BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS BASE DRACHMA LOAN RATE TO 17.5PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus said on Monday</p>
<p>it is cutting its base drachma lending rate by 125 basis points</p>
<p>to 17.50 percent effective October 1.</p>
<p>It is also lowering its floating mortgage rate by 25 basis</p>
<p>points to 15.75 percent.</p>
<p>The bank said rates for housing renovation loans will come</p>
<p>down 100 basis points to 21 percent while consumer loan rates</p>
<p>will stay unchanged at 23 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus offered the following deposit rates:</p>
<p>** Simple savings account: 11.50 percent</p>
<p>** Time deposits: rates up to 12.50 percent</p>
<p>** CYPROFIT monthly income account: annual yield 12.40</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
